## Original Content
The primary runoff in South Carolina between Sen. Darline Graham and Rep. Ralph Norman is another test of President Trump's influence. He's backing Darline, sister of the late Sen. Lindsey Graham.

## Summary
The South Carolina senate runoff election between Sen. Darline Graham and Rep. Ralph Norman is a test of President Trump's political influence, as he endorses Graham. Darline Graham is the sister of the late Sen. Lindsey Graham, adding a familial connection to the race.

## Key Points
- The runoff election serves as a test of President Trump's endorsement power in politics.
- President Trump is supporting Sen. Darline Graham in the election.
- Darline Graham has a notable familial link as the sister of the late Sen. Lindsey Graham.
- Rep. Ralph Norman is the opposing candidate in the primary runoff.
- This election reflects ongoing intra-party dynamics, likely within the Republican Party.


